{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":64663,"duration_api_ms":64537,"num_turns":3,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"86493607-e980-4dad-a24d-c83781b0caf6","total_cost_usd":0.3071417,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22758,"cache_read_input_tokens":77091,"output_tokens":802,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22758,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":802,"cacheReadInputTokens":77091,"cacheCreationInputTokens":22758,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.200853,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":70,"outputTokens":4144,"cacheReadInputTokens":275837,"cacheCreationInputTokens":46332,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1062887,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Both amendments address verified code quality issues: a confirmed identical duplicate function and an inconsistent API usage pattern. Both are straightforward, low-risk improvements that reduce maintenance burden and improve consistency.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-d6a4b57a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: concentration_from_total() in nitrogen_cycle.rs (lines 383-389) is byte-for-byte identical to concentration() in water.rs (lines 301-307). Both perform the same NaN/Inf check, EPSILON threshold, and non-negativity clamping. This is a real DRY violation — if the safety logic is updated in one copy (e.g., to handle a new edge case like subnormal floats), the other silently diverges, creating a latent correctness bug. Extracting to a single pub(crate) function is straightforward and eliminates this risk."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-4a64f0c3","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: algae_growth.rs is the only system file that calls state.water.tan_mg_n_per_l(volume_l) directly, bypassing the ConcentrationView abstraction. All other consumers (plant_growth.rs, shrimp.rs, events.rs, snapshot.rs) use state.concentrations(). The inconsistency means algae_growth.rs computes volume_l separately and passes it manually, while the canonical pattern computes it once inside ConcentrationView via water_volume_l(). Standardizing to state.concentrations() ensures volume is always computed through the same canonical path, reduces coupling to WaterState internals, and makes the calling convention uniform across all systems. The refactoring is mechanical and low-risk."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ea9146a7-d068-4d89-84e3-f11ea4fe75ef"}
